                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "306f1eda-ac0a-3f65-adf1-957e2d27b2db",
                        "entry_id": "0710076c-4bd6-3d3e-a549-51d3b486d691",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un peuple de tribus errantes dans le desert de Namib en Namibie (Afrique)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "756f1aec-e36d-4ac2-a7bc-1eb6ab38026c",
                                "sense_id": "306f1eda-ac0a-3f65-adf1-957e2d27b2db",
                                "text": "Ce voyageur indifférent, c’était un chasseur bushman, un beau type de cette vaillante race aux yeux vifs, aux gestes rapides, dont la vie nomade se passe dans les bois ^([1])."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78b7fd23-c116-3a1c-aa9a-cdd3e29cfb14",
                        "entry_id": "0710076c-4bd6-3d3e-a549-51d3b486d691",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un homme qui vit dans, ou a une forte expérience dans le bush australien, l’outback."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ef0c0e6-ded1-4eca-8bf0-8ddbca6afb7e",
                        "source_entry_id": "0710076c-4bd6-3d3e-a549-51d3b486d691",
                        "source_sense_description": "habitant de l'outback australien",
                        "target_lang_word": "bushman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bushman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8720956c-29b9-36ae-bdcf-a656e2bb0030",
                                        "entry_id": "dd466548-49d6-3bf9-9c05-4194bae1d64f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who lives in or has extensive experience of the Australian bush or outback."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b30fb2b1-16e9-4861-80db-b52d12be8f89",
                                                "sense_id": "8720956c-29b9-36ae-bdcf-a656e2bb0030",
                                                "text": "To A. B. Paterson, son of a dispossessed squatter, writing from a city office, the bushmen with their horses and simple skills were the backbone of Australia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0df79b50-9e0a-4469-ae5b-a24b38e3624c",
                                                "sense_id": "8720956c-29b9-36ae-bdcf-a656e2bb0030",
                                                "text": "Its^([the Bulletin's]) writers shaped ‘a group myth about Australians and their destiny’; in the absence of conventional heroes, visiting the past to claim the bushman as the first ‘Australian’, the anti-hero in the struggles against empire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea0f1ac2-f927-4cb1-add5-184207b26418",
                                                "sense_id": "8720956c-29b9-36ae-bdcf-a656e2bb0030",
                                                "text": "Later, historian Russel Ward (1958) famously identified the outback bushman as the “typical” Australian – a rugged individualist, courageous and loyal to his mates."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
